-- The DEONTIC-VERDICT exhibit for the DMN exporter (R13, spec §16).
--
-- A guarded chain whose row bodies are all deontic arms does not refuse any
-- more: it lowers to a VERDICT decision table over its guards, each rule's
-- output a string naming the arm. The obligation semantics
-- (PARTY/MUST/WITHIN/HENCE/LEST) are the BPMN exporter's job; a BPMN gateway
-- consumes the verdict to choose the process path.
--
-- One decide per shape the lowering must pin:
--
--   * `reporting duty`      the generic verdict chain, off-corpus: MUST,
--                           FULFILLED, MAY, SHANT and MUST+HENCE arms in one
--                           chain, exercising every `verdictOf` spelling —
--                           including the HENCE self-call, whose edge must
--                           NOT survive into the DRG (the verdict table's
--                           requirements are its guards, R13 × R11), and
--                           whose self-recursion keeps the decide
--                           safety-refused (D-PARTIAL, verdict-aware form);
--   * `joint duty`          the NEGATIVE control for the v1 scope: an arm
--                           that is RAND of two obligations is not a single
--                           deontic arm, so the chain keeps today's
--                           RegulativeBody refusal (D-LITERALEXPR Blocking);
--   * `bare duty`           the other negative control: a bare deontic body
--                           is not a guarded chain at all and keeps
--                           NotAGuardedChain (D-LITERALEXPR Blocking).
--
-- The two controls are module-called (`invoked …`) so §2.5.6 rule 3 does not
-- drop them before they can refuse — same device as
-- not-ok/dated-chain-regulative.l4.
--
-- The heading below is load-bearing: `l4 export --to=dmn` with no
-- `--model-name` takes the model name from the outermost `§`.

IMPORT prelude

§ `deontic verdict`

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Issuer

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    `file the termination report`
    `file the annual report`
    `publish a notice`
    `advertise the offering`
    `file jointly`
    `notify investors`

GIVEN `may terminate`       IS A BOOLEAN
      cycles                IS A NUMBER
      `notice window open`  IS A BOOLEAN
      escalated             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`reporting duty` `may terminate` cycles `notice window open` escalated MEANS
    IF   `may terminate`
    THEN PARTY Issuer MUST `file the termination report` WITHIN 5
    ELSE IF   cycles AT MOST 0
         THEN FULFILLED
         ELSE IF   `notice window open`
              THEN PARTY Issuer MAY `publish a notice`
              ELSE IF   escalated
                   THEN PARTY Issuer SHANT `advertise the offering`
                   ELSE PARTY Issuer MUST `file the annual report` WITHIN 30
                        HENCE `reporting duty` `may terminate` (cycles MINUS 1) `notice window open` escalated

-- v1-scope negative control: RAND of two obligations is not a single arm.
GIVEN trigger IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`joint duty` trigger MEANS
    IF   trigger
    THEN (PARTY Issuer MUST `file jointly` WITHIN 5
          RAND PARTY Issuer MUST `notify investors` WITHIN 5)
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN trigger IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`invoked joint duty` trigger MEANS `joint duty` trigger

-- the other negative control: a bare deontic body is not a chain.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bare duty` MEANS PARTY Issuer MUST `notify investors` WITHIN 10

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`invoked bare duty` MEANS `bare duty`
